# Secret key used to hash repo names before they're written to loc_cache.json.
# Generate one with: python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
#
# Copy this file to .env (already gitignored) and fill in the real value.
# Also add the same value as a repo secret named CACHE_HMAC_KEY on GitHub
# (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions) so the daily workflow derives
# the exact same cache keys -- otherwise every run rehashes everything and the
# incremental LOC cache stops paying off.
CACHE_HMAC_KEY=
